    \item[{Note}]
  \par
The result of the substitution may be either an absolute or a relative URI reference. In the latter case it is combined with the value of {\itshape xml:base} in force at the place where the {\itshape cRef} attribute occurs to form an absolute URI in the usual manner as prescribed by \xref{https://www.w3.org/TR/xmlbase/}{XML Base}.
    \item[{Example}]
  \leavevmode\bgroup\exampleFont \begin{shaded}\noindent\mbox{}{<\textbf{cRefPattern}\hspace*{6pt}{matchPattern}="{([1-9A-Za-z]+)⃥s+([0-9]+):([0-9]+)}"\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{replacementPattern}="{\#xpath(//div[@type='book'][@n='\$1']/div[@type='chap'][@n='\$2']/div[@type='verse'][@n='\$3'])}"/>}\end{shaded}\egroup 


