    \item[{Note}]
  \par
May contain character data and phrase-level elements. Typical values will be of the form \textit{nominative}, \textit{accusative}, \textit{dative}, \textit{genitive}, etc.\par
This element is synonymous with <gram type="case">.
    \item[{Example}]
  Taken from \textit{Wörterbuch der Deutschen Sprache. Veranstaltet und herausgegeben von Joachim Heinrich Campe. Erster Theil. A - bis - E. (Braunschweig 1807. In der Schulbuchhandlung)}: 
\begin{quote}Das Evangelium, des Evangelii, ...\end{quote}
\leavevmode\bgroup\exampleFont \begin{shaded}\noindent\mbox{}{<\textbf{entry}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{form}\hspace*{6pt}{type}="{lemma}">}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{gramGrp}>}\mbox{}\newline 
