    \item[@calendar]
  indicates one or more systems or calendars to which the date represented by the content of this element belongs.
\begin{reflist}
    \item[\xref{http://www.tei-c.org/Activities/Council/Working/tcw27.xml}{Deprecated}]
  will be removed on 2024-11-11
    \item[{Status}]
  Optional
    \item[{Datatype}]
  1–∞ occurrences of \hyperref[TEI.teidata.pointer]{teidata.pointer} separated by whitespace
    \item[{Schematron}]
   <sch:rule context="tei:*[@calendar]"> <sch:assert test="string-length( normalize-space(.) ) gt 0"> @calendar indicates one or more  systems or calendars to which the date represented by the content of this element belongs,  but this <sch:name/> element has no textual content.</sch:assert> </sch:rule>
\end{reflist}  
    \item[@fromUnit]
  indicates a source unit of measure that is to be converted into another unit indicated in {\itshape toUnit}.
\begin{reflist}
    \item[{Status}]
  Required
    \item[{Datatype}]
  \hyperref[TEI.teidata.pointer]{teidata.pointer}
\end{reflist}  
    \item[@toUnit]
  the target unit of measurement for a conversion from a source unit referenced in {\itshape fromUnit}.
\begin{reflist}
    \item[{Status}]
  Required
    \item[{Datatype}]
  \hyperref[TEI.teidata.pointer]{teidata.pointer}
\end{reflist}  
\end{sansreflist}  
    \item[{Contained by}]
  
    \item[header: ]
   \hyperref[TEI.unitDef]{unitDef}
    \item[{May contain}]
  Empty element
    \item[{Note}]
  \par
The conversion element is designed to store information about converting from one unit of measurement to another. The {\itshape formula} attribute holds an XPath expression that indicates how the measurement system in {\itshape fromUnit} is converted to the system in {\itshape toUnit}. Do not confuse the usage of the dating attributes ({\itshape from} and {\itshape to}) in the examples with the attributes ({\itshape fromUnit} and {\itshape toUnit}) designed to reference units of measure.
    \item[{Example}]
  \leavevmode\bgroup\exampleFont \begin{shaded}\noindent\mbox{}{<\textbf{conversion}\hspace*{6pt}{formula}="{\$fromUnit * 12}"\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{from}="{1707}"\hspace*{6pt}{fromUnit}="{\#shilling}"\hspace*{6pt}{to}="{1971}"\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{toUnit}="{\#pence}"/>}\end{shaded}\egroup 


    \item[{Example}]
  \leavevmode\bgroup\exampleFont \begin{shaded}\noindent\mbox{}{<\textbf{conversion}\hspace*{6pt}{formula}="{\$fromUnit * 20}"\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{from}="{1701}"\hspace*{6pt}{fromUnit}="{\#pound}"\hspace*{6pt}{to}="{1971}"\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{toUnit}="{\#shilling}"/>}\end{shaded}\egroup 


    \item[{Content model}]
  \fbox{\ttfamily <content>\newline
 <empty/>\newline
</content>\newline
    } 
    \item[{Schema Declaration}]
  \mbox{}\hfill\\[-10pt]\begin{Verbatim}[fontsize=\small]
element conversion
{
   tei_att.global.attributes,
   tei_att.datable.attributes,
   tei_att.formula.attributes,
   tei_att.locatable.attributes,
   attribute calendar { list { + } }?,
   attribute fromUnit { text },
   attribute toUnit { text },
   empty
}
\end{Verbatim}

\end{reflist}  \index{corr=<corr>|oddindex}
\begin{reflist}
\item[]\begin{specHead}{TEI.corr}{<corr> }(correction) contains the correct form of a passage apparently erroneous in the copy text. [\xref{https://www.tei-c.org/release/doc/tei-p5-doc/en/html/CO.html\#COEDCOR}{3.5.1. Apparent Errors}]\end{specHead} 
    \item[{Module}]
  core
