    \item[{Note}]
  \par
Both the beginning and ending of the deleted sequence must be marked: the beginning by the \hyperref[TEI.delSpan]{<delSpan>} element, the ending by the target of the {\itshape spanTo} attribute.\par
The text deleted must be at least partially legible, in order for the encoder to be able to transcribe it. If it is not legible at all, the \hyperref[TEI.delSpan]{<delSpan>} tag should not be used. Rather, the \hyperref[TEI.gap]{<gap>} tag should be employed to signal that text cannot be transcribed, with the value of the {\itshape reason} attribute giving the cause for the omission from the transcription as deletion. If it is not fully legible, the \hyperref[TEI.unclear]{<unclear>} element should be used to signal the areas of text which cannot be read with confidence. See further sections \xref{https://www.tei-c.org/release/doc/tei-p5-doc/en/html/PH.html\#PHOM}{12.3.1.7. Text Omitted from or Supplied in the Transcription} and, for the close association of the \hyperref[TEI.delSpan]{<delSpan>} tag with the \hyperref[TEI.gap]{<gap>}, \hyperref[TEI.damage]{<damage>}, \hyperref[TEI.unclear]{<unclear>} and \hyperref[TEI.supplied]{<supplied>} elements, \xref{https://www.tei-c.org/release/doc/tei-p5-doc/en/html/PH.html\#PHCOMB}{12.3.3.2. Use of the gap, del, damage, unclear, and supplied Elements in Combination}.\par
The \hyperref[TEI.delSpan]{<delSpan>} tag should not be used for deletions made by editors or encoders. In these cases, either the \hyperref[TEI.corr]{<corr>} tag or the \hyperref[TEI.gap]{<gap>} tag should be used.
    \item[{Example}]
  \leavevmode\bgroup\exampleFont \begin{shaded}\noindent\mbox{}{<\textbf{p}>}Paragraph partially deleted. This is the undeleted\mbox{}\newline 
 portion {<\textbf{delSpan}\hspace*{6pt}{spanTo}="{\#a23}"/>}and this the deleted\mbox{}\newline 
 portion of the paragraph.{</\textbf{p}>}\mbox{}\newline 
{<\textbf{p}>}Paragraph deleted together with adjacent material.{</\textbf{p}>}\mbox{}\newline 
{<\textbf{p}>}Second fully deleted paragraph.{</\textbf{p}>}\mbox{}\newline 
{<\textbf{p}>}Paragraph partially deleted; in the middle of this\mbox{}\newline 
 paragraph the deletion ends and the anchor point marks\mbox{}\newline 
 the resumption {<\textbf{anchor}\hspace*{6pt}{xml:id}="{a23}"/>} of the text. ...{</\textbf{p}>}\end{shaded}\egroup 


