\end{itemize} \hfil\\[-10pt]\begin{sansreflist}
    \item[@columns]
  (columns) specifies the number of columns per page
\begin{reflist}
    \item[{Status}]
  Optional
    \item[{Datatype}]
  1–2 occurrences of \hyperref[TEI.teidata.count]{teidata.count} separated by whitespace
    \item[{Note}]
  \par
If a single number is given, all pages referenced have this number of columns. If two numbers are given, the number of columns per page varies between the values supplied. Where {\itshape columns} is omitted the number is assumed to be 1.\par
Columns may be independent of page orientation or reading direction, and a single textual {\itshape stream} may have one or more columns.
\end{reflist}  
    \item[@streams]
  (textual streams) indicates the number of streams per page, each of which contains an independent textual stream
\begin{reflist}
    \item[{Status}]
  Optional
    \item[{Datatype}]
  1–2 occurrences of \hyperref[TEI.teidata.count]{teidata.count} separated by whitespace
    \item[{Note}]
  \par
If a single number is given, all pages referenced have this number of textual streams. If two numbers are given, the number of textual streams per page varies between the values supplied. Where {\itshape streams} is omitted the number is assumed to be 1 and unless specified elsewhere the script orientation of the source is identical to that used in the TEI document.
\end{reflist}  
    \item[@ruledLines]
  (ruled lines) specifies the number of ruled lines per column
\begin{reflist}
    \item[{Status}]
  Optional
    \item[{Datatype}]
  1–2 occurrences of \hyperref[TEI.teidata.count]{teidata.count} separated by whitespace
    \item[{Note}]
  \par
If a single number is given, all columns have this number of ruled lines. If two numbers are given, the number of ruled lines per column varies between the values supplied.
\end{reflist}  
    \item[@writtenLines]
  (written lines) specifies the number of written lines per column
\begin{reflist}
    \item[{Status}]
  Optional
    \item[{Datatype}]
  1–2 occurrences of \hyperref[TEI.teidata.count]{teidata.count} separated by whitespace
    \item[{Note}]
  \par
If a single number is given, all columns have this number of written lines. If two numbers are given, the number of written lines per column varies between the values supplied.
\end{reflist}  
\end{sansreflist}  
