    \item[@function]
  describes the function or use of the material in relation to the object as a whole.
\begin{reflist}
    \item[{Status}]
  Optional
    \item[{Datatype}]
  \hyperref[TEI.teidata.enumerated]{teidata.enumerated}
    \item[{Sample values include:}]
  \begin{description}

\item[{binding}]covering material of a codex
\item[{endband}]sewing at the head or tail of the codex spine to strengthen the binding, often decorative
\item[{slipcase}]removable protective cover for a set of one or more codices
\item[{support}]the surface for writing
\item[{tie}]a ribbon or string used to bind or close a codex or rolled scroll
\end{description} 
    \item[{Note}]
  \par
The sample values here are for descriptive bibliography. Other sets of sample values might include armrests, legs, tabletop, pan, and back for furniture; or wall, floor, window, column, ceiling, roof, stairs, chimney for architecture.
\end{reflist}  
    \item[@target]
