    \item[{Note}]
  \par
May be used to indicate that a passage is distinguished from the surrounding text for reasons concerning which no claim is made. When used in this manner, \hyperref[TEI.q]{<q>} may be thought of as syntactic sugar for \hyperref[TEI.hi]{<hi>} with a value of {\itshape rend} that indicates the use of such mechanisms as quotation marks.
    \item[{Example}]
  \leavevmode\bgroup\exampleFont \begin{shaded}\noindent\mbox{}It is spelled {<\textbf{q}>}Tübingen{</\textbf{q}>} — to enter the\mbox{}\newline 
 letter {<\textbf{q}>}u{</\textbf{q}>} with an umlaut hold down the {<\textbf{q}>}option{</\textbf{q}>} key and press \mbox{}\newline 
{<\textbf{q}>}0 0 f c{</\textbf{q}>}\end{shaded}\egroup 


