    \item[{Note}]
  \par
May contain character data mixed with any other elements defined in the dictionary tag set.\par
Identical in sub-elements to an \hyperref[TEI.entry]{<entry>} tag, and used where a dictionary has embedded information inside one entry which could have formed a separate entry. Some authorities distinguish related entries, run-on entries, and various other types of degenerate entries; no such typology is attempted here.
    \item[{Example}]
  The following example from \textit{Webster's New Collegiate Dictionary (Springfield, Mass.: G. \& C. Merriam Company, 1975)} shows a single related entry for which no definition is given, since its meaning is held to be readily derivable from the root entry:\leavevmode\bgroup\exampleFont \begin{shaded}\noindent\mbox{}{<\textbf{entry}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{form}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{orth}>}neu·ral{</\textbf{orth}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{pron}>}'n(y)ūr-əl{</\textbf{pron}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{</\textbf{form}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{gramGrp}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{pos}>}adj{</\textbf{pos}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{</\textbf{gramGrp}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{sense}\hspace*{6pt}{n}="{1}">}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{def}>}of, relating to, or affecting a nerve or the nervous system{</\textbf{def}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{</\textbf{sense}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{sense}\hspace*{6pt}{n}="{2}">} ... {</\textbf{sense}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{entry}\hspace*{6pt}{type}="{relatedEntry}">}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{form}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{orth}>}neurally{</\textbf{orth}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{pron}\hspace*{6pt}{extent}="{suff}">}-ə-lē{</\textbf{pron}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{</\textbf{form}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{gramGrp}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{pos}>}adv{</\textbf{pos}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{</\textbf{gramGrp}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{</\textbf{entry}>}\mbox{}\newline 
{</\textbf{entry}>}\end{shaded}\egroup 


    \item[{Example}]
  The following example from \textit{Diccionario de la Universidad de Chicago Inglés-Español y Español-Inglés / The University of Chicago Spanish Dictionary, Fourth Edition, compiled by Carlos Castillo and Otto F. Bond (Chicago: University of Chicago Press, 1987)} shows a number of related entries embedded in the main entry. The original entry resembles the following:
\begin{quote}{\bfseries abeja} [a·bé·xa]{\itshape f.} bee;{\bfseries abejera} [a·be·xé·ra]{\itshape f.} beehive;{\bfseries abejón} [a·be·xóon]{\itshape m.} drone; bumblebee;{\bfseries abejorro} [a·be·xó·rro]{\itshape m.} bumble bee.\end{quote}
 One encoding for this entry would be:\leavevmode\bgroup\exampleFont \begin{shaded}\noindent\mbox{}{<\textbf{entry}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{form}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{orth}>}abeja{</\textbf{orth}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{</\textbf{form}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{gramGrp}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{gen}>}f. {</\textbf{gen}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{</\textbf{gramGrp}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{sense}\hspace*{6pt}{n}="{1.}">}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{usg}\hspace*{6pt}{type}="{domain}">} (ento.) {</\textbf{usg}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{def}>} bee {</\textbf{def}>}. {</\textbf{sense}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{sense}\hspace*{6pt}{n}="{2.}">}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{def}>} busy bee, hard worker {</\textbf{def}>}. {</\textbf{sense}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{sense}\hspace*{6pt}{n}="{3.}">}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{usg}\hspace*{6pt}{orig}="{A.}"\hspace*{6pt}{type}="{domain}">} (astron.) {</\textbf{usg}>}, {<\textbf{def}>} Musca {</\textbf{def}>} — {</\textbf{sense}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{entry}\hspace*{6pt}{type}="{relatedEntry}">}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{form}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{orth}\hspace*{6pt}{orig}="{a. albanila}">} abeja albanila {</\textbf{orth}>}, {</\textbf{form}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{sense}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{def}>}mason bee{</\textbf{def}>};{</\textbf{sense}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{</\textbf{entry}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{entry}\hspace*{6pt}{type}="{relatedEntry}">}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{form}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{orth}\hspace*{6pt}{orig}="{a. carpintera}">} abeja carpintera {</\textbf{orth}>}, {</\textbf{form}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{sense}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{def}>}carpenter bee {</\textbf{def}>};{</\textbf{sense}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{</\textbf{entry}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{entry}\hspace*{6pt}{type}="{relatedEntry}">}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{form}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{orth}\hspace*{6pt}{orig}="{a. reina or maestra}"\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{xml:id}="{re-o3}">} abeja reina {</\textbf{orth}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{orth}\hspace*{6pt}{mergedIn}="{\#re-o4}">} abeja maestra {</\textbf{orth}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{</\textbf{form}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{sense}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{def}>} queen bee {</\textbf{def}>};{</\textbf{sense}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{</\textbf{entry}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{entry}\hspace*{6pt}{type}="{relatedEntry}">}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{form}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{orth}\hspace*{6pt}{orig}="{a. neutra or obrera}"\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{xml:id}="{re-o4}">} abeja neutra {</\textbf{orth}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{orth}\hspace*{6pt}{mergedIn}="{\#re-o3}">} abeja obrera {</\textbf{orth}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{</\textbf{form}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{sense}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{def}>}worker bee{</\textbf{def}>}.{</\textbf{sense}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{</\textbf{entry}>}\mbox{}\newline 
{</\textbf{entry}>}\end{shaded}\egroup 


    \item[{Example}]
  In the much larger Simon \& Schuster Spanish-English dictionary (\textit{Tana de Gámez, ed., Simon and Schuster's International Dictionary (New York: Simon and Schuster, 1973).}) these derived forms of \textit{abeja} are treated as separate main entries, but there are other embedded phrases shown as \hyperref[TEI.re]{<re>}s in its main entry for \textit{abeja}:
\begin{quote}abeja, f. 1. (ento.) bee. 2. busy bee, hard worker. 3. (astron.) A., Musca. — a. albanila, mason bee; a. carpintera, carpenter bee; a. reina or maestra, queen bee; a. neutra or obrera, worker bee.\end{quote}
 This entry may be encoded thus:\leavevmode\bgroup\exampleFont \begin{shaded}\noindent\mbox{}{<\textbf{entry}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{form}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{orth}>}abeja{</\textbf{orth}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{</\textbf{form}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{gramGrp}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{gen}>}f.{</\textbf{gen}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{</\textbf{gramGrp}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{sense}\hspace*{6pt}{n}="{1.}">}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{usg}\hspace*{6pt}{type}="{domain}">}(ento.){</\textbf{usg}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{def}>}bee{</\textbf{def}>}. {</\textbf{sense}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{sense}\hspace*{6pt}{n}="{2.}">}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{def}>}busy bee, hard worker{</\textbf{def}>}. {</\textbf{sense}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{sense}\hspace*{6pt}{n}="{3.}">}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{usg}\hspace*{6pt}{orig}="{A.}"\hspace*{6pt}{type}="{domain}">}(astron.){</\textbf{usg}>}, {<\textbf{def}>}Musca{</\textbf{def}>} — {</\textbf{sense}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{entry}\hspace*{6pt}{type}="{relatedEntry}">}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{form}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{orth}\hspace*{6pt}{orig}="{a. albanila}">}abeja albanila{</\textbf{orth}>}, {</\textbf{form}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{sense}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{def}>}mason bee{</\textbf{def}>}; {</\textbf{sense}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{</\textbf{entry}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{entry}\hspace*{6pt}{type}="{relatedEntry}">}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{form}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{orth}\hspace*{6pt}{orig}="{a. carpintera}">}abeja carpintera{</\textbf{orth}>}, {</\textbf{form}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{sense}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{def}>}carpenter bee{</\textbf{def}>}; {</\textbf{sense}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{</\textbf{entry}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{entry}\hspace*{6pt}{type}="{relatedEntry}">}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{form}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{orth}\hspace*{6pt}{orig}="{a. reina or maestra}"\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{xml:id}="{re-o1}">}abeja reina{</\textbf{orth}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{orth}\hspace*{6pt}{mergedIn}="{\#re-o1}">}abeja maestra{</\textbf{orth}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{</\textbf{form}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{sense}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{def}>}queen bee{</\textbf{def}>}; {</\textbf{sense}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{</\textbf{entry}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{entry}\hspace*{6pt}{type}="{relatedEntry}">}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{form}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{orth}\hspace*{6pt}{orig}="{a. neutra or obrera}"\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{xml:id}="{re-o2}">}abeja neutra{</\textbf{orth}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{orth}\hspace*{6pt}{mergedIn}="{\#re-o2}">}abeja obrera{</\textbf{orth}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{</\textbf{form}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{sense}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{def}>}worker bee{</\textbf{def}>}. {</\textbf{sense}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{</\textbf{entry}>}\mbox{}\newline 
{</\textbf{entry}>}\end{shaded}\egroup 


    \item[{Content model}]
  \mbox{}\hfill\\[-10pt]\begin{Verbatim}[fontsize=\small]
<content>
 <alternate maxOccurs="unbounded"
  minOccurs="0">
  <textNode/>
  <classRef key="model.gLike"/>
