    \item[@locus]
  indicates the specific aspect of the encoding (markup or content) for which responsibility is being assigned.
\begin{reflist}
    \item[{Status}]
  Required
    \item[{Datatype}]
  1–∞ occurrences of \hyperref[TEI.teidata.enumerated]{teidata.enumerated} separated by whitespace
    \item[{Legal values are:}]
  \begin{description}

\item[{name}]responsibility is being assigned concerning the name of the element or attribute used.
\item[{start}]responsibility is being assigned concerning the start of the element concerned.
\item[{end}]responsibility is being assigned concerning the end of the element concerned.
\item[{location}]responsibility is being assigned concerning the location of the element concerned.
\item[{value}]responsibility is being assigned concerning the content (for an element) or the value (for an attribute)
\end{description} 
\end{reflist}  
\end{sansreflist}  
