    \item[core: ]
   \hyperref[TEI.desc]{desc}
    \item[{Note}]
  \par
The \hyperref[TEI.respons]{<respons>} element is designed for cases in which fine-grained information about specific aspects of the markup of a text is desirable for whatever reason. Global responsibility for certain aspects of markup is usually more simply indicated in the TEI header, using the \hyperref[TEI.respStmt]{<respStmt>} element within the title statement, edition statement, or change log.
    \item[{Example}]
  \leavevmode\bgroup\exampleFont \begin{shaded}\noindent\mbox{}{<\textbf{respons}\hspace*{6pt}{locus}="{name location}"\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{resp}="{\#encoder1}"\hspace*{6pt}{target}="{\#p1}"/>}\mbox{}\newline 
{<\textbf{respons}\hspace*{6pt}{locus}="{value}"\hspace*{6pt}{match}="{@rend}"\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{resp}="{\#encoder2}"\hspace*{6pt}{target}="{\#p2}"/>}\mbox{}\newline 
{<\textbf{list}\hspace*{6pt}{type}="{encoders}">}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{item}\hspace*{6pt}{xml:id}="{encoder1}"/>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{item}\hspace*{6pt}{xml:id}="{encoder2}"/>}\mbox{}\newline 
{</\textbf{list}>}\end{shaded}\egroup 


    \item[{Example}]
  In this (partially fictional) example the entire document was transcribed and encoded by a single encoder, except for one passage which was transcribed and encoded by the proofreader.\leavevmode\bgroup\exampleFont \begin{shaded}\noindent\mbox{}\mbox{}\newline 
\textit{<!-- in the <teiHeader>: -->}{<\textbf{respStmt}\hspace*{6pt}{xml:id}="{enc01}">}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{name}>}C. Colin Backslash{</\textbf{name}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{resp}>}transcription{</\textbf{resp}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{resp}>}encoding{</\textbf{resp}>}\mbox{}\newline 
{</\textbf{respStmt}>}\mbox{}\newline 
{<\textbf{respStmt}\hspace*{6pt}{xml:id}="{prf01}">}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{name}>}Erin Spelling{</\textbf{name}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{resp}>}proofreading{</\textbf{resp}>}\mbox{}\newline 
{</\textbf{respStmt}>}\mbox{}\newline 
