    \item[{Note}]
  \par
Where the {\itshape place} attribute is not provided on the \hyperref[TEI.rt]{<rt>} element, the default assumption is that the ruby gloss is above where the text is horizontal, and to the right of the text where it is vertical.
    \item[{Example}]
  The word \textit{大統領} \textit{daitōryō} (president) is glossed character by character in hiragana to provide a pronunciation guide.\leavevmode\bgroup\exampleFont \begin{shaded}\noindent\mbox{}{<\textbf{p}\hspace*{6pt}{style}="{writing-mode: vertical-rl}"\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{xml:lang}="{ja}">}\mbox{}\newline 
\textit{<!--{\textJapanese {...}}-->}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{ruby}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{rb}>}{\textJapanese {大}}{</\textbf{rb}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{rt}\hspace*{6pt}{place}="{right}">}{\textJapanese {だい}}{</\textbf{rt}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{</\textbf{ruby}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{ruby}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{rb}>}{\textJapanese {統}}{</\textbf{rb}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{rt}\hspace*{6pt}{place}="{right}">}{\textJapanese {とう}}{</\textbf{rt}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{</\textbf{ruby}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{ruby}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{rb}>}{\textJapanese {領}}{</\textbf{rb}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}\hspace*{6pt}{<\textbf{rt}\hspace*{6pt}{place}="{right}">}{\textJapanese {りょう}}{</\textbf{rt}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\hspace*{6pt}{</\textbf{ruby}>}\mbox{}\newline 
\textit{<!--{\textJapanese {...}}-->}\mbox{}\newline 
{</\textbf{p}>}\end{shaded}\egroup 


