    \item[{Note}]
  \par
The same element is used for all cases of uncertainty in the transcription of element content, whether for written or spoken material. For other aspects of certainty, uncertainty, and reliability of tagging and transcription, see chapter \xref{https://www.tei-c.org/release/doc/tei-p5-doc/en/html/CE.html\#CE}{22. Certainty, Precision, and Responsibility}.\par
The \hyperref[TEI.damage]{<damage>}, \hyperref[TEI.gap]{<gap>}, \hyperref[TEI.del]{<del>}, \hyperref[TEI.unclear]{<unclear>} and \hyperref[TEI.supplied]{<supplied>} elements may be closely allied in use. See section \xref{https://www.tei-c.org/release/doc/tei-p5-doc/en/html/PH.html\#PHCOMB}{12.3.3.2. Use of the gap, del, damage, unclear, and supplied Elements in Combination} for discussion of which element is appropriate for which circumstance.\par
The {\itshape hand} attribute points to a definition of the hand concerned, as further discussed in section \xref{https://www.tei-c.org/release/doc/tei-p5-doc/en/html/PH.html\#PHDH}{12.3.2.1. Document Hands}.
    \item[{Example}]
  \leavevmode\bgroup\exampleFont \begin{shaded}\noindent\mbox{}{<\textbf{u}>} ...and then {<\textbf{unclear}\hspace*{6pt}{reason}="{background-noise}">}Nathalie{</\textbf{unclear}>} said ... {</\textbf{u}>}\end{shaded}\egroup 


    \item[{Content model}]
  \mbox{}\hfill\\[-10pt]\begin{Verbatim}[fontsize=\small]
<content>
 <macroRef key="macro.paraContent"/>
</content>
    
\end{Verbatim}

    \item[{Schema Declaration}]
  \mbox{}\hfill\\[-10pt]\begin{Verbatim}[fontsize=\small]
element unclear
{
   tei_att.global.attributes,
   tei_att.editLike.attributes,
   tei_att.dimensions.attributes,
   tei_att.cmc.attributes,
   attribute reason
   {
      list
      {
         (
            "illegible"
          | "inaudible"
          | "faded"
          | "background_noise"
          | "eccentric_ductus"
         )+
      }
   }?,
   attribute agent { text }?,
   tei_macro.paraContent}
\end{Verbatim}

\end{reflist}  \index{undo=<undo>|oddindex}\index{target=@target!<undo>|oddindex}
