    \item[@absolute]
  supplies an absolute value for the time.
\begin{reflist}
    \item[{Status}]
  Optional
    \item[{Datatype}]
  \hyperref[TEI.teidata.temporal.w3c]{teidata.temporal.w3c}
    \item[{Note}]
  \par
This attribute should always be specified on a \hyperref[TEI.when]{<when>} element which serves as the target for the {\itshape origin} attribute of a \hyperref[TEI.timeline]{<timeline>}.
\end{reflist}  
    \item[@unit]
  specifies the unit of time in which the {\itshape interval} value is expressed, if this is not inherited from the parent \hyperref[TEI.timeline]{<timeline>}.
\begin{reflist}
    \item[{Status}]
  Optional
    \item[{Datatype}]
  \hyperref[TEI.teidata.enumerated]{teidata.enumerated}
    \item[{Suggested values include:}]
  \begin{description}

\item[{d}](days)
\item[{h}](hours)
\item[{min}](minutes)
\item[{s}](seconds)
\item[{ms}](milliseconds)
\end{description} 
\end{reflist}  
    \item[@interval]
  specifies a time interval either as a number or as one of the keywords defined by the datatype \textsf{teidata.interval}
\begin{reflist}
    \item[{Status}]
  Optional
    \item[{Datatype}]
  \hyperref[TEI.teidata.interval]{teidata.interval}
\end{reflist}  
    \item[@since]
  identifies the reference point for determining the time of the current \hyperref[TEI.when]{<when>} element, which is obtained by adding the interval to the time of the reference point.
\begin{reflist}
    \item[{Status}]
  Optional
    \item[{Datatype}]
  \hyperref[TEI.teidata.pointer]{teidata.pointer}
    \item[{Note}]
  \par
This attribute should point to another \hyperref[TEI.when]{<when>} element in the same \hyperref[TEI.timeline]{<timeline>}. If no value is supplied, and the {\itshape absolute} attribute is also unspecified, then the reference point is understood to be the origin of the enclosing \hyperref[TEI.timeline]{<timeline>} tag.
\end{reflist}  
\end{sansreflist}  
    \item[{Contained by}]
  
    \item[linking: ]
   \hyperref[TEI.timeline]{timeline}
    \item[{May contain}]
  Empty element
    \item[{Note}]
  \par
On this element, the global {\itshape xml:id} attribute must be supplied to specify an identifier for this point in time. The value used may be chosen freely provided that it is unique within the document and is a syntactically valid name. There is no requirement for values containing numbers to be in sequence.
    \item[{Example}]
  \leavevmode\bgroup\exampleFont \begin{shaded}\noindent\mbox{}{<\textbf{when}\hspace*{6pt}{interval}="{20}"\hspace*{6pt}{since}="{\#w2}"\hspace*{6pt}{xml:id}="{TW3}"/>}\end{shaded}\egroup 


    \item[{Content model}]
  \fbox{\ttfamily <content>\newline
 <empty/>\newline
</content>\newline
    } 
